#-- Class 2

"Prose is architecture, not interior decoration, and the Baroque is over"; Strong structure; Simple!;
Importance of headings, subheadings and topic sentences reflect your writing strategy;
Establis emphasis;
Link ideas;
Hierarchy should be very clear!;
One paragraph for each major idea; Lead sentence of each paragraph should be a robust topic sentence;
Topic sentence begins the paragraph; and end it in conformity with the beginning;
As a rule, avoid 1, 2, or even 3 sentence paragraphs; Avoid fragmentation...;
Transition words to connect independent sentences;
Try writing independent sentences and connecting!;
Language: clear, simple, declarative sentences;
Be specific, avoid empty generalities;
Avoid stacking adjectives (check her example, is great!);
Go to active voice (subject does the actions); Methods sometimes needs passive voice;
Put statements in positive form (avoid "not");
Remove "the fact that"; Remove "There is", "There are", "It is" (existential phrases);
Data WERE gathered (not was);
Weak vs. strong verbs: We made (performed, conducted) the arrangment for / We arranged (verb changed to a noun);
Keep the action in the verb!;
Read sentences aloud (read as a reader); If you take a breath is too long;
Subject - Verb - O positioning, close as possible;
Avoid "Late Verbs", keep them in the beginning;

